==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|modifien}}, from {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|modifier}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|modificare||to limit, control, regulate, deponent}}, from {{m|la|modificari||to measure off, set bound to, moderate}}, from {{m|la|modus||measure}} + {{m|la|facere||to make}}; see {{m|en|mode}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-modify.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{IPA|mɒdɪfaɪ̯|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|modif|ies}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[make]] partial [[change]]s to.
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[be]] or [[become]] modified.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|adapt}}, {{l|en|alter}}, {{l|en|amend}}, {{l|en|revamp}}, {{l|en|rework}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|modification}}
* {{l|en|modifier}}

